„­bible_version£KJV¤book§chapter¨sections™…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ°And when king Arad the Canaanite, which dwelt in the south, heard tell that Israel came by the way of the spies; then he fought against Israel, and took some of them prisoners.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd Israel vowed a vow unto the LORD, and said, If thou wilt indeed deliver this people into my hand, then I will utterly destroy their cities.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ­And the LORD hearkened to the voice of Israel, and delivered up the Canaanites; and they utterly destroyed them and their cities: and he called the name of the place Hormah.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses“„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd they journeyed from mount Hor by the way of the Red sea, to compass the land of Edom: and the soul of the people was much discouraged because of the way.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÖAnd the people spake against God, and against Moses, Wherefore have ye brought us up out of Egypt to die in the wilderness? for there is no bread, neither is there any water; and our soul loatheth this light bread.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙkAnd the LORD sent fiery serpents among the people, and they bit the people; and much people of Israel died.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses‘„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÑTherefore the people came to Moses, and said, We have sinned, for we have spoken against the LORD, and against thee; pray unto the LORD, that he take away the serpents from us. And Moses prayed for the people.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse	¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¯And the LORD said unto Moses, Make thee a fiery serpent, and set it upon a pole: and it shall come to pass, that every one that is bitten, when he looketh upon it, shall live.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤And Moses made a serpent of brass, and put it upon a pole, and it came to pass, that if a serpent had bitten any man, when he beheld the serpent of brass, he lived.¦layout ªlast_verse	…¤book§chapter«first_verse
