„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙwAnd they journeyed from Oboth, and pitched at Ije-abarim, in the wilderness which is before Moab, toward the sunrising.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ=From thence they removed, and pitched in the valley of Zared.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËFrom thence they removed, and pitched on the other side of Arnon, which is in the wilderness that cometh out of the coasts of the Amorites: for Arnon is the border of Moab, between Moab and the Amorites.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ9Wherefore it is said in the book of the wars of the LORD,¦layout ‚¤text»What he did in the Red sea,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text»And in the brooks of Arnon,¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤text¿And at the stream of the brooks¦layout ‚¤textÙ&That goeth down to the dwelling of Ar,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ"And lieth upon the border of Moab.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙAnd from thence they went to Beer: that is the well whereof the LORD spake unto Moses, Gather the people together, and I will give them water.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines’‚¤text»Then Israel sang this song,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#Spring up, O well; sing ye unto it:¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤text¼The princes digged the well,¦layout ‚¤textÙ#The nobles of the people digged it,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ4By the direction of the lawgiver, with their staves.¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ.And from the wilderness they went to Mattanah:¦layout©paragraphªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ;and from Mattanah to Nahaliel: and from Nahaliel to Bamoth:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsand from Bamoth in the valley, that is in the country of Moab, to the top of Pisgah, which looketh toward Jeshimon.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙCAnd Israel sent messengers unto Sihon king of the Amorites, saying,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÎLet me pass through thy land: we will not turn into the fields, or into the vineyards; we will not drink of the waters of the well: but we will go along by the king's high way, until we be past thy borders.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙËAnd Sihon would not suffer Israel to pass through his border: but Sihon gathered all his people together, and went out against Israel into the wilderness: and he came to Jahaz, and fought against Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ´And Israel smote him with the edge of the sword, and possessed his land from Arnon unto Jabbok, even unto the children of Ammon: for the border of the children of Ammon was strong.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And Israel took all these cities: and Israel dwelt in all the cities of the Amorites, in Heshbon, and in all the villages thereof.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤For Heshbon was the city of Sihon the king of the Amorites, who had fought against the former king of Moab, and taken all his land out of his hand, even unto Arnon.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse ¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines“‚¤textÙ*Wherefore they that speak in proverbs say,¦layout ‚¤text²Come into Heshbon,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ,Let the city of Sihon be built and prepared:¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines”‚¤textÙ(For there is a fire gone out of Heshbon,¦layout ‚¤text¿A flame from the city of Sihon:¦layout§quote_1‚¤text¼It hath consumed Ar of Moab,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ*And the lords of the high places of Arnon.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines•‚¤text²Woe to thee, Moab!¦layout ‚¤textÙ%Thou art undone, O people of Chemosh:¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ$He hath given his sons that escaped,¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ!And his daughters, into captivity¦layout§quote_1‚¤textÙ Unto Sihon king of the Amorites.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines“‚¤textÙ:We have shot at them; Heshbon is perished even unto Dibon,¦layout ‚¤textÙ-And we have laid them waste even unto Nophah,¦layout§quote_1‚¤text»Which reacheth unto Medeba.¦layout§quote_1ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.Thus Israel dwelt in the land of the Amorites.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd Moses sent to spy out Jaazer, and they took the villages thereof, and drove out the Amorites that were there.¦layout ªlast_verse …¤book§chapter«first_verse!ªlast_verse#¦verses“„¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’And they turned and went up by the way of Bashan: and Og the king of Bashan went out against them, he, and all his people, to the battle at Edrei.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÕAnd the LORD said unto Moses, Fear him not: for I have delivered him into thy hand, and all his people, and his land; and thou shalt do to him as thou didst unto Sihon king of the Amorites, which dwelt at Heshbon.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvSo they smote him, and his sons, and all his people, until there was none left him alive: and they possessed his land.¦layout ªlast_verse#